B.bYE=s(['1. Check if the thermostat screen is blank or showing "Low Battery" \xe2\u20ac\u201d replace the 2 AA/AAA batteries inside the faceplate.',"2. Verify the mode is set to HEAT (above current room temp) or COOL (below current room temp).","3. Check that the furnace service switch (looks like a light switch near the unit) wasn't accidentally flipped off.","4. Inspect the air filter; a heavily clogged filter can trip the high-limit safety switch."],t.s)
B.aFh=new A.ua("hvac_no_heat_cool","Furnace or AC Not Responding to Thermostat",B.bYE,"Fresh thermostat batteries / mode adjustment restored heating/cooling!")
B.c_J=s(["1. A single chirp every 30\xe2\u20ac\u201c60 seconds indicates a low 9V or AA backup battery (or end-of-life sensor).","2. Twist the detector counter-clockwise off its ceiling bracket, swap in a fresh alkaline battery, and hold the HUSH/TEST button for 5 seconds.","3. WARNING: If the CO alarm sounds 4 rapid beeps continuously, evacuate immediately and call emergency services."],t.s)
